      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "1. PUBLISH FLOW (Developer → Registry)\n   Developer → 'superbox push' → Security scanners (5-step) → S3 Registry (metadata JSON)\n\n2. DISCOVER FLOW (User → Frontend)\n   User → Frontend UI → Backend API → S3 (fetch mcp.json) → Display server cards\n\n3. CONFIGURE FLOW (Developer → IDE)\n   Developer → 'superbox pull --client vscode' → Backend API → S3 metadata → Write MCP config\n   → VS Code reads config with proxy.py command\n\n4. EXECUTION FLOW (IDE → Lambda → MCP Server)\n   VS Code → proxy.py (stdio-WS bridge) → API Gateway WS → Lambda ($connect)\n   → Clone repo → Install deps → Start MCP subprocess → Ready\n   User query → VS Code → proxy stdin → WS → Lambda → MCP server stdin\n   → MCP executes tool → stdout → Lambda → WS → proxy stdout → VS Code → User\n\n5. MONITORING FLOW (Developer → CloudWatch)\n   Developer → 'superbox logs --name X' → CloudWatch Logs API → Display execution logs",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. PUBLISH FLOW (Developer → Registry)\n   Developer → 'superbox push' → Security scanners (5-step) → S3 Registry (metadata JSON)\n\n2. DISCOVER FLOW (User → Frontend)\n   User → Frontend UI → Backend API → S3 (fetch mcp.json) → Display server cards\n\n3. CONFIGURE FLOW (Developer → IDE)\n   Developer → 'superbox pull --client vscode' → Backend API → S3 metadata → Write MCP config\n   → VS Code reads config with proxy.py command\n\n4. EXECUTION FLOW (IDE → Lambda → MCP Server)\n   VS Code → proxy.py (stdio-WS bridge) → API Gateway WS → Lambda ($connect)\n   → Clone repo → Install deps → Start MCP subprocess → Ready\n   User query → VS Code → proxy stdin → WS → Lambda → MCP server stdin\n   → MCP executes tool → stdout → Lambda → WS → proxy stdout → VS Code → User\n\n5. MONITORING FLOW (Developer → CloudWatch)\n   Developer → 'superbox logs --name X' → CloudWatch Logs API → Display execution logs",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 263
    },
